# Image-model artifacts: these belong on NAS, never in Git.
# The directory patterns are anchored to the repository root on purpose. These
# are names of domain areas too, so an unanchored pattern would silently
# swallow source directories such as
# packages/python/domain/src/image_model_lab_domain/artifacts/.
# Nested paths are covered by suffix instead of by directory name: the suffix
# patterns below, and tools/repo_policy.py, which rejects weights, media, logs
# and key material at any depth, plus oversized files and secrets. A rule
# keyed on a directory name would hit the same trap, since a UI or module
# directory can legitimately be called logs/ or models/.
/artifacts/
/datasets/
/models/
/outputs/
/checkpoints/
/logs/
*.log
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.avif
*.gif
*.mp4
*.webm

# Explicitly allow tiny documentation assets if added intentionally
!docs/**/*.png
!docs/**/*.jpg
!docs/**/*.jpeg
!docs/**/*.webp
